        "original_id": "f3b53b86-3e7a-547f-911d-99c269f4ad1e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Steve Denton, Albert Costa, Johan Kriek\n- Events: 1982 Australian Open – Men's Singles\n- Places: Kingsville, Texas\n- Organizations: ATP Tour\n- Topics: Tennis\n\nFacts:\n- Steve Denton was born on September 5, 1956, in Kingsville, Texas.\n- Albert Costa began playing tennis at the age of five.\n- Steve Denton became a professional tennis player on the ATP Tour and is a former player.\n- Johan Kriek was the defending champion in the 1982 Australian Open – Men's Singles.\n- Johan Kriek defeated Steve Denton 6–3, 6–3, 6–2 in the final of the 1982 Australian Open – Men's Singles.\n- Johan Kriek successfully defended his title and won the Men's Singles title at the 1982 Australian Open.\n- The 1982 Australian Open – Men's Singles final between Johan Kriek and Steve Denton was a rematch of the previous year.",
